## Canvas vendor libraries (embedded, served at `/vendor/`)

- **Location:** `crates/slices/jinn-canvas/resources/vendor/` — each
  library's license file ships inside its directory, byte-verbatim from
  the upstream distribution, embedded by the same `include_bytes!`
  table as the library itself and served at `/vendor/<lib>/LICENSE`.
  Versions are pinned row-by-row in `vendor-manifest.toml` beside them.
- **Licenses:** per library below. All permit redistribution and
  conveys the license text with the copy — which the served tree does
  by construction.

| Library | npm package | Version | License | Upstream |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Chart.js | `chart.js` | 4.6.1 | MIT | https://github.com/chartjs/Chart.js |
| D3 | `d3` | 7.9.0 | ISC | https://github.com/d3/d3 |
| highlight.js | `@highlightjs/cdn-assets` | 11.12.0 | BSD-3-Clause | https://github.com/highlightjs/highlight.js |
| KaTeX (+fonts) | `katex` | 0.19.1 | MIT | https://github.com/KaTeX/KaTeX |
| Mermaid | `mermaid` | 12.2.0 | MIT | https://github.com/mermaid-js/mermaid |
| Observable Plot | `@observablehq/plot` | 0.6.17 | ISC | https://github.com/observablehq/plot |
| p5.js | `p5` | 1.11.13 | LGPL-2.1 | https://github.com/processing/p5.js |
| Preact + htm | `preact`, `htm` | 3.1.1 | Apache-2.0 (both) | https://github.com/preactjs/preact, https://github.com/developit/htm |
| uPlot | `uplot` | 1.6.32 | MIT | https://github.com/leeoniya/uPlot |
| Vega | `vega` | 6.4.0 | BSD-3-Clause | https://github.com/vega/vega |
| Vega-Lite | `vega-lite` | 6.5.0 | BSD-3-Clause | https://github.com/vega/vega-lite |
| vega-embed | `vega-embed` | 7.3.0 | BSD-3-Clause | https://github.com/vega/vega-embed |
| Vue | `vue` | 3.5.44 | MIT | https://github.com/vuejs/core |
| matter.js | `matter-js` | 0.20.0 | MIT | https://github.com/liabru/matter-js |
| three.js (+addons) | `three` | 0.185.0 | MIT | https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js |

`canvas.css` in the same tree is jinn's own work (AGPL-3.0, like the
rest of jinn) — it is authored, not vendored, and carries no upstream
license file.

Preact/htm note: the served `preact/` directory holds the
`@download/preact-standalone` bundle (preact + htm + hooks compiled
together) and one Apache-2.0 license file covering both works; the
distribution's license file is the bundled one, kept verbatim.

three.js note: the served `three/` directory holds the minified core
module build plus a subtree of addon modules (controls, loaders,
parametric geometries, buffer/skeleton utilities) under
`three/addons/`, all from the single `three` npm package; one MIT
license file covers core and addons alike.
